# ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST. This file used to name what to leave out, and
# an independent review found eight gitignored paths it had missed - two of
# which (scan_universe.csv, scan_log.csv.superseded) were shipping into a
# registry already, with .streamlit/secrets.toml and calls.csv latent the
# moment those files existed.
#
# That is the wrong default for a repository that holds holdings, targets,
# a broking session token and a scan log. `COPY . .` means anything not
# excluded ships, so the exclusion list has to be exhaustive - and it will
# not stay exhaustive, because personal files arrive without anyone
# remembering to come back here.
#
# So: exclude everything, then name the few things the feed needs. A new
# CSV of positions is now excluded because nobody added it, rather than
# included because nobody removed it.
#
# The cost is that a genuinely new dependency must be added below. That is
# a build failure, which is loud, rather than a data leak, which is not.

**

# Every Python module, at any depth. Broad on purpose: the feed's import
# chain is config, instruments, kite_client, kite_ticker, live_bars,
# market_source, bar_store and object_store today, but hand-listing those
# would mean a future import produces an image that builds and then dies
# on start. Source is a few hundred KB; the risk is not worth the saving.
!**/*.py

# The feed's dependency list, installed before the source is copied.
!requirements-feed.txt

# The instrument snapshot: tokens and the F&O set that universe() needs.
# Named as one file rather than the directory so a stray .tmp beside it
# cannot ride along.
!instruments/universe.json

# Tests are source, and are the one kind of source this image never runs.
test_*.py

# Not secret, but it describes the account, subnets and security group,
# and it has no business inside a container with outbound network access.
deploy/**
